# unit-tests.list: kvm-unit-tests' tests in the KVM suite, one a line: the
# test's name in x86/unittests.cfg, what corpus.sh requires of it under
# Rach2's KVM, Linux's result on the testing PC, and the reason. EXPECT is
# `pass`; `skip`, the test's own skip for what the processor or QEMU lacks, as
# Linux skips it there, with its reason; `fail`, where Linux fails and Rach2
# is to fail as it does; or `excluded`, not run, for one of the reasons the
# stack's approved plan allows. A test whose result is the processor's has
# FLAG?A:B there: A on a processor whose `flags` in /proc/cpuinfo have FLAG
# and B on one without it. LINUX is the result of Linux 6.18.58, WSL's,
# with QEMU 10.2.1 and kernel-irqchip=split, as ref/linux-unit-tests.txt has
# it: a row Linux failed there expects a pass unless its EXPECT is `fail`, and
# names Linux's failure after `Linux:`. Inside a machine of KVM, as the KVM
# suite's cases run, FLAG `outer_kvm` holds: there `debug` and `xapic` are
# excluded and `hyperv_connections`, `la57`, `pcid-disabled` and `x2apic`
# fail, as under Linux 6.12 as the host of the same machine
# (dev-log/81-kvm/81-25.md). Under another hypervisor, as under the Mac's
# TCG, `access` is excluded and `debug` fails, as under Linux there. A test
# is expected to fail only where Linux as the host of the same machine fails
# it, and its row names how.
#
# NAME EXPECT LINUX REASON
access outer_kvm?pass:hypervisor?excluded:pass pass not run under another hypervisor, as under the Mac's TCG, where each of the 4,915,200 permutations of a level that set a reserved bit fails with QEMU TCG's error code 8 for 9, the P bit of a reserved-bit fault's left out, under Linux 6.12 as the host too, each failure some 223 bytes at two serial exits a byte, and neither host ends: on one processor Linux printed about 23 failures a second and Rach2 16, some 2.5 days a level at Linux's rate (dev-log/84-locks/84-88.md)
access-reduced-maxphyaddr skip skip /sys/module/kvm_intel/parameters/allow_smaller_maxphyaddr not equal to Y
access_fep skip skip Forced emulation prefix (FEP) not available
asyncpf excluded pass asynchronous page faults, deferred by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10 to a later milestone
cet skip skip No CET features supported
cmpxchg8b excluded skip i386: built only for i386, and the staged tests are x86-64's
debug outer_kvm?excluded:hypervisor?fail:pass fail Linux: unhandled #PF at ffff0ff0 and 404fb8; not run inside a machine of KVM, where Linux 6.12 as the host did not finish it in 900 s, after its MOVSS-blocking single step (dev-log/81-kvm/81-25.md); under another hypervisor, as under the Mac's TCG, fails MOV SS + watchpoint + ICEBP, 24 of 25 passing, as under Linux 6.12 as the host there
emulator pass pass
ept excluded skip nested virtualization, excluded by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10: Rach2's KVM gives its guests neither SVM nor VMX
ept-mbec excluded skip nested virtualization, excluded by the owner's decision of 2026-11-10: Rach2's KVM gives its guests neither SVM nor VMX
eventinj pass pass
hypercall pass pass
hyperv_clock pass pass
hyperv_connections outer_kvm?fail:pass fail Linux: 7 tests, 1 unexpected failures; inside a machine of KVM fails receive pending message: 0/2, as under Linux 6.12 as the host of the same machine (dev-log/84-locks/84-33.md)
hyperv_stimer pass pass
hyperv_stimer_direct pass pass
hyperv_synic pass pass
idt_test pass pass
intel_iommu pass pass
ioapic pass pass
kvmclock_test pass pass
la57 outer_kvm?fail:pass fail Linux: la57.c:230: assert failed: write_cr4_safe(read_cr4() | X86_CR4_PCIDE) == 0, as under Linux 6.12 as the host inside a machine of KVM
lam pass pass
memory pass pass
msr pass pass
msr64 pass pass
pcid-asymmetric pass pass
pcid-disabled outer_kvm?fail:pass fail Linux: FAIL: Test on INVPCID when disabled, as under Linux 6.12 as the host inside a machine of KVM
pcid-enabled pass pass
pks skip skip PKS not enabled: the processor has no PKS
pku skip skip PKU not enabled
pmu kvm_pmu?hypervisor?fail:pass:skip fail Linux: AMD's overflow subtests fail, 7 to 10 of 10 by turns; under a hypervisor whose own work on each exit the counters count, the counts and overflows fail on Linux 6.12 too; skips without a host PMU, which its config requires
pmu_lbr kvm_lbr?pass:skip skip Linux's on the testing PC, which offers no LBR format; the Lenovo's Debian passes it with Haswell's 16 records
pmu_pebs skip skip Linux's on the testing PC; PEBS is not offered, and the Lenovo's Debian reference settles Intel's
rdpru pass pass
realmode pass pass
rmap_chain pass pass
s3 pass pass
setjmp pass pass
sieve pass pass
smap smap?pass:skip pass SMAP not enabled, on a processor without it, as the Lenovo's i3-4030U
smptest pass pass
smptest3 pass pass
